-- title:
--   A coercive polynomial is nonnegative iff it is nonnegative where its gradient vanishes
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a real polynomial in $n$ variables that is **coercive**: $p(x_k)\to+\infty$ for every sequence $(x_k)$ in $\mathbb R^n$ with $\|x_k\|\to+\infty$. Then
--   $$
--   p(x)\ge0\ \ \forall x\in\mathbb R^n\quad\Longleftrightarrow\quad p(x)\ge0\ \ \text{for every }x\in\mathbb R^n\text{ with }\nabla p(x)=0 .
--   $$
--
--   This reduces the nonnegativity of the polynomial of Theorem 3.2 to its coercivity, claim (3.2.1), and its nonnegativity at critical points, claim (3.2.2).
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - encoding: coercive: f(xₖ) → +∞ along every sequence with ‖xₖ‖ → +∞ → Tendsto (fun x => eval x p) (cocompact (Fin n → ℝ)) atTop; reason: in finite dimension the cocompact filter is generated by complements of bounded sets, so the two definitions coincide
--   - encoding: ∇p(x) = 0 → ∀ i, eval x (pderiv i p) = 0; reason: the formal partial derivatives of a polynomial are its partial derivatives
-- source:
--   Ahmadi, Dibek & Hall, Sums of Separable and Quadratic Polynomials, arXiv:2105.04766v1, Theorem 3.2, proof, p.10

import Mathlib

open MvPolynomial Filter

namespace SPQPoly

/-- **A coercive polynomial is nonnegative iff it is nonnegative where its gradient vanishes.**
Ahmadi, Dibek & Hall, *Sums of Separable and Quadratic Polynomials*, arXiv:2105.04766v1, Theorem 3.2, proof, p.10:
"It follows that a coercive polynomial is nonnegative if and only if it is nonnegative at the
points where its gradient vanishes." Coercive is defined there: "a function f : Rn → R is
coercive if for every sequence {xk} with {||xk||} → +∞, we have {f(xk)} → +∞."

**Formalization Note.** `ℝⁿ` is `Fin n → ℝ`. Coercivity is
`Tendsto (fun x => eval x p) (cocompact _) atTop`; in finite dimension the cocompact filter is the
filter of complements of bounded sets, so this is the sequence definition of the page. The
gradient vanishing at `x` is `∀ i, eval x (pderiv i p) = 0`. -/
theorem coercive_nonneg_iff_critical {n : ℕ} (p : MvPolynomial (Fin n) ℝ)
    (hp : Tendsto (fun x : Fin n → ℝ => eval x p) (cocompact (Fin n → ℝ)) atTop) :
    (∀ x : Fin n → ℝ, 0 ≤ eval x p) ↔
      (∀ x : Fin n → ℝ, (∀ i : Fin n, eval x (pderiv i p) = 0) → 0 ≤ eval x p) := by sorry

end SPQPoly
